# Code owners for the legacy-proxy shim.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the default owner comes first and the team
# folders override it below. Each team owns its folder in BOTH places it exists:
#
#   dis-to-legacy/teams/<team>/       the service definitions, identical everywhere
#   dis-to-legacy/envs/<env>/<team>/  that team's weights for one environment
#
# That pairing is the point: a team can shift its own traffic in one environment
# without platform review, and platform keeps everything else -- platform/, the
# env kustomizations that say which teams are present, and CI.

# Default owner: everything not claimed by a team folder below.
*                                       @Altinn/team-platform

# autorisasjon
/dis-to-legacy/teams/autorisasjon/      @altinn/team-access-management
/dis-to-legacy/envs/*/autorisasjon/     @altinn/team-access-management

# core
/dis-to-legacy/teams/core/              @altinn/team-core
/dis-to-legacy/envs/*/core/             @altinn/team-core

# studio
/dis-to-legacy/teams/studio/            @altinn/team-altinn-studio
/dis-to-legacy/envs/*/studio/           @altinn/team-altinn-studio

# dis-poc is the platform team's own proof of concept; it routes onto the canary
# in platform/dummy rather than a real migrated app. Covered by the default
# owner above, listed here so the set of team folders stays complete.
/dis-to-legacy/teams/dis-poc/           @Altinn/team-platform
/dis-to-legacy/envs/*/dis-poc/          @Altinn/team-platform
